<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ssang Gi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 956–958</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Shuang Ji</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ssang Gi was a Chinese official of the Later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a> who came to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> with an embassy in 956 and stayed in the service of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gwangjong-of-goryeo">King Gwangjong</a> of Goryeo. On his advice Goryeo introduced civil service examinations on the Chinese model in 958, and he supervised the first of them. The examinations became a lasting basis of Korean bureaucracy.</p></div>
